{
  "message": "Good news: the local emulation passed for design revision 2, so we know the bucket's upload, read and delete calls work against a stand-in storage server. The catch is that this stand-in doesn't check the most important rules, like who has permission, blocking public access and Google's own region checks, so the security requirements are still untested and need a real Terraform plan or a test in a Google Cloud project to prove them. There's nothing in the diagram to fix right now, but one thing decides where we go next: does the data have to stay in Australia, or is australia-southeast1 just a convenient default for this test?",
